{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/15087-sell-me-on-the-god-machine","id":15087,"title":"Sell me on the God-Machine","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-20T20:31:31-08:00","id":15087,"title":"Sell me on the God-Machine","content":"Or at least help me grok it. As I said in another thread, I'm so far from grokking it, I think I actively korg it. And that's not even a good neologism like grok.<br /> <br /> I don't mean the mechanisms of Infrastructure, which is pretty well-explained in terms of Occult Matrices in chapter 1 of the Demon text and can be mapped to a lot of gnostic demiurge/reality-cancer concepts that aren't necessarily The God Machine.<br /> <br /> I mean the what and why of the GM itself, this thing that can warp space and time but<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">can't breach a thin layer of rock to provide oil to an array of machines that's somehow been waiting for that to happen for millions of years</div></div> </div> </div> in one of the God-Machine Chronicle story seeds<br /> <br /> I don't find that kind of mysterious inconsistency mysterious, just irksome. It's like the GM is at once too big and powerful to fight, and yet too weak and dependent on nigh-coincidence to take basic care of itself - so how does it exist as a threat in the first place?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1096,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","user":"squidheadjax","date":". 11-20-2013, 11:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T20:54:51-08:00","id":15099,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>squidheadjax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/15087-sell-me-on-the-god-machine#post15087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean the what and why of the GM itself, this thing that can warp space and time but<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">can't breach a thin layer of rock to provide oil to an array of machines that's somehow been waiting for that to happen for millions of years</div></div> </div> </div> in one of the God-Machine Chronicle story seeds</div> </div> </div> </div>One fundamental assumption error and one outright failure to read.<br /> <br /> 1. &quot;Can warp space and time&quot; <i>in the right places and at the right times with the right Infrastructure in place to do so</i> is not the same thing as &quot;Can warp space and time everywhere at all times without any conditions.&quot;<br /> <br /> 2. Let's read carefully now:</span></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> He was content to continue with the rig\u2019s original function for a time, but <b>then the God-Machine found it had need of the platform.</b> It moved the drill slightly and pushed down into the sea bed, seeking to uncover something <b>left buried for millions of years</b> (see Blueprints). </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the drill continues unabated, it eventually opens a cavern below the sea floor. Therein lies an exposed section of the God-Machine that <b>hasn\u2019t been in operation for millennia.</b> It requires the oil above it to work, meaning that if the drill reaches this cavern, the God-Machine pulls the oil from the deposit and then comes to life, absorbing the drill and the cables and assimilating the rig itself. </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I have toys in my basement that I haven't played with in years. Some of them require batteries to operate that have long since run down. I am fully capable of going down there and digging those toys out and putting fresh batteries in them, but:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">a) I'm lazy and haven't been in the relevant part of the basement for years, so I'll probably ask a family member who's more familiar with the area to get them out of storage, and</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u200bb) I'm lazy and the moment I put batteries into those toys I am kind of obligated to play with them before the batteries run out again, which I probably won't do unless I have to entertain my baby cousins over Thanksgiving, so I'll probably put off digging the toys out for as long as possible until Thanksgiving is around the corner and I know my baby cousins are coming with my aunt to visit and I will have to keep the little squirts occupied while my parents catch up with their sibling/in-law.</span><br /> <br /> Make sense?</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 11-21-2013, 12:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T22:23:15-08:00","id":15130,"title":"","content":"I mean the what and why of the GM itself, this thing that can warp space and time but<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">can't breach a thin layer of rock to provide oil to an array of machines that's somehow been waiting for that to happen for millions of years</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">It can and it does (tries to). The platform is the godmachine's infrastructure to do so; all the time-bending stuff also requires infrastructure. In my interpretation, the breaching of the rock layer is something very located and physical, so the required infrastructure has similar properties. Warping time and space may require a more abstract and strange infrastructure.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1125-gflash","name":"gflash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1125_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T23:32:47-08:00","id":15175,"title":"","content":"Satchel, are you actually intending to say that the only reason the God-Machine isn't in full control of everything is self-defeating lassitude?<br /> <br /> Thank you gflash, that was less condescending. It's not the specific configuration of Infrastructure - which makes great sense as its own story, <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Just replace the neglected Infrastructure with some other horror beneath the rig and you don't need the God-machine. Especially not a God-Machine that apparently couldn't be arsed to keep its own body in working order.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The way it comes across to me is that the conditions are so incredibly <i>contingent</i> that it seems that the God-Machine's only real power is to eff the supposedly ineffable and riff on strange power confluences that nothing else can understand - and then it fails to eff not even the supernatural forces but the plain old mortals who come in to eff things up, sometimes managing to catch an eff of the ineffable themselves in the process.<br /> <br /> The more I think on it, the more I end up with a <i>disappointed</i> view of the God-machine. It seems to know just enough and have just enough agency that its failures can break the world but it can barely keep itself running, much less stay in good working order. From a perspective outside the setting, I don't feel a sense of victory at the thought of defeating the God-Machine, I feel like I'd be kicking the universe's biggest puppy for messing up the carpet when it didn't know better. Except the carpet is usually human (and sort-of-human) lives, so better do it anyway. It's not like the character knows anything other than to be scared of what happens if the seemingly-godlike machine succeeds (or worse, fails spectacularly).<br /> <br /> Maybe that's actually the way it's supposed to be? I guess it would fit the overall themes of the World of Darkness. Everything is broken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T00:50:40-08:00","id":15212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>squidheadjax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/15087-sell-me-on-the-god-machine?p=15175#post15175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Satchel, are you actually intending to say that the only reason the God-Machine isn't in full control of everything is self-defeating lassitude?</div> </div> </div> </div>I am saying the Machine is a Big Fuckin' Thing that has finite resources to allocate to systems that it does not have need of at all times but which it would be more trouble to rebuild than to put it in whatever form of storage takes the least strain to use. The thing's juggling It-only-knows how many projects at any given time and no small number of those use gears that consume resources to keep running. Big Infrastructure runs on ever smaller sets of Infrastructure and at least one class of supernatural entity is actively fucking with things at the micro level and necessitating correction or abandonment and option-assessment.<br /> <br /> Multiply the problem of running out of fossil fuels by a few orders of magnitude on top of the rocket-fuel-to-move-your-rocket-fuel logistical conundrum and the issues the God-Machine has to work with concerning basic physics even after building in exceptions make a fair amount of sense.<br /> <br /> I do apologize that my use of an analogical metaphor rang condescending to you, but yes, &quot;everything is broken&quot; is about the size of it. Remember the tagline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T06:41:08-08:00","id":15337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>squidheadjax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/15087-sell-me-on-the-god-machine#post15087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or at least help me grok it. As I said in another thread, I'm so far from grokking it, I think I actively korg it. And that's not even a good neologism like grok.<br /> <br /> I don't mean the mechanisms of Infrastructure, which is pretty well-explained in terms of Occult Matrices in chapter 1 of the Demon text and can be mapped to a lot of gnostic demiurge/reality-cancer concepts that aren't necessarily The God Machine.<br /> <br /> I mean the what and why of the GM itself, this thing that can warp space and time but<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">can't breach a thin layer of rock to provide oil to an array of machines that's somehow been waiting for that to happen for millions of years</div></div> </div> </div> in one of the God-Machine Chronicle story seeds<br /> <br /> I don't find that kind of mysterious inconsistency mysterious, just irksome. It's like the GM is at once too big and powerful to fight, and yet too weak and dependent on nigh-coincidence to take basic care of itself - so how does it exist as a threat in the first place?</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not sure I get your question, but remember that the GMC does not work on a human time scale, and works mostly through &quot;objects&quot; already in motion. So when it needed fossil fuel, it ensured humans started extracting that from the ground. The amount of energy needed to reshape space and time is huge, the amount needed to nudge a human to go drill for oil is very little. The GMC would rather wait a few thousand extra years before using the fuel than waste energy to do it now, unless the need is huge. And here the unknowable comes in:<br /> <br /> The GMC is likely doing a cost/benefit analysis on the concept of just using angels or other parts under it's direct control to get fuel for Infrastructure vs. using &quot;incidental&quot; human activity. Obviously, the energy needed to do the former was to high compared to the benefit In other words, if time is not an issue, the GMC will always do the most energy economical action possible. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1228-jhiriit","name":"Jhiriit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T09:05:38-08:00","id":15410,"title":"","content":"The God-Machine has two major goals: survival and growth. I'm going to focus on survival, since it'll be basically be the same.<br /> <br /> It's already surviving, it's just needs to maintain that. Maintaining survival means building up redundant infrastructure, and keeping enough delicate processes on hand to make timely adjustments. That's the status quo it strives for. Things working as intended. All lights green. All systems go. Optimal operating procedure. This means the world and its physics continue to function as well know it. Including some of the supernatural elements we've come to know and love.<br /> <br /> Which might be good, but maybe not. Maybe the world would be a lot cooler, a lot less <i>of Darkness,</i> if we should shed this pseudospiritual parasite. Since there are entities (demons, stigmatics, hunters, <i>player characters)</i> possibly working toward that goal, maintenance is the primary goal of the GM. It knows what it needs to do to accomplish this goal: infrastructure, infrastructure, infrastructure. And so it puts its existing infrastructure to work creating additional infrastructure (yo dawg, etc etc etc). To do that, it might need to repurpose things. Or use components its been sitting on.<br /> <br /> Example: The GM needs an angel that isn't a hunter angel to make some small component in, say, a factory that's infrastructure. Let's say, some kind of <i>builder</i> angel. A maker angel. The only angel in the area? Of course its a hunter angel. So it calculates the most viable options:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>It can stop maintaining the hunter angel's cover, and use it for the new angel. That might later require additional infrastructure to adjust to fit. Then there's a hunter angel wandering around without a cover, which is not efficient.</li> <li>It could try to use the inappropriate angel to make this thing, but <i>that</i> might require additional support. And the potential for disaster is very high.</li> <li>Dispose of that angel and use the aether budgeted for the hunter angel's purposes to bring a new, appropriate angel and cover into being.</li> </ol>For the sake of argument, it finds 3 is most efficient as far as resources. The infrastructure to do this exists, and the aether is already budgeted. It just needs to get rid of the angel. Fortunately, that hunter angel had been trailing a whole posse of demons, and requesting backup. There's no way it can challenge the whole ring on its own and survive. So the GM tells it to proceed with the plan. There are three outcomes, all acceptable.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>The angel somehow wins. A different kind of victory, and definitely the worst outcome, but it's still furthering the GM's goals.</li> <li>The angel totally fails. It is obliterated without harming one demon in any way. Furthering the GM's goals! Now it can create its builder angel.</li> <li>The angel partially succeeds, destroying or damaging some of the ring, and perishing. GM's goals met plus bonus.</li> </ol>From the demon (<i>player character)</i> angle, it looks like a single, unprepared angel has attempt to catch them off guard. This doesn't make any sense! The Destroyer took demonic form, and pounded the hunter angel's face off. It cost him his cover, but they all survived! What a <i>stuuuupid</i> angel, goddamn. <br /> <br /> Elsewhere, that unused aether (and a bunch of subtly manipulated infrastructure) goes into the newly freed-up RAM slot, and a new, purpose-filled angel steps out. It makes a thing, implants it, and the GM's new redundant back-up comes online, which is far more important than a single hunter angel. A special bonus, this ring of Unchained is weary now, and they aren't going after infrastructure for a while. Or they <i>are</i>, but they're way cocky. A win for the GM in either case.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17-metrophelean","name":"Metrophelean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T09:27:40-08:00","id":15433,"title":"","content":"Option 4. The angel realises with horror that the God-Machine doesn't actually care one way or the other about its success. The angel's mission is, therefore irrelevant. It Falls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T10:02:26-08:00","id":15448,"title":"","content":"I guess being a programmer gives me basically automatic understanding of this unknowable thing, haha. Well consider it an operating system, one that responds to various input and output capabilities similar to any other operating system. It has scheduled tasks that it performs, automatic updates, things of that nature. I'm sure everyone knows how that goes. Now take it a step further and think that not only does it do software updates, but tells when hardware updates are necessary and when to unplug unnecessary systems.<br /> <br /> That is basically what the God Machine is, but with a little more sentience than that... or just the same amount (It could be very well simply running a program that was long before executed that may have run amok).<br /> <br /> The God Machine isn't GOD, it simply has similar capabilities when running the appropriate programs due to precise infrastructure (You try running high quality games with a bad graphics card). It could have been Made by God, Aliens, Spirits, King Kong, Godzilla or Cthulhu, but it is still a Machine. Its simply a machine with major capabilities that impact the entire world depending on what function call has been made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T14:46:35-08:00","id":15637,"title":"","content":"Hmmm. Better. Not much I can offer in reply right now that would amount to 'sure, neat'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T14:56:18-08:00","id":15644,"title":"","content":"Hmmm. Better. Not much I can offer in reply right now that would amount to something other than 'sure, neat'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T15:01:48-08:00","id":15648,"title":"","content":"It's an unknowable and ineffable God that is decidedly not loving and sinister, though not necessarily outright malevolent (and protects itself and therefore earth from some apocalypses, like Y2K f'r instance), it's the secret behind the world in a conspiracy-theory kinda way that lets you play Call of Cthulhu-style adventures or Matrix-style adventures.<br /> <br /> It can link in to any of the gamelines and their cosmologies (some more easily than others - Promethean and changeling being easier, vampire and Mummy being harder IMO). It can catapult you off into sci-fi - it's an alien computer! A machine built by future-humans! The result of a transhumanist Singularity that all of humankind coalesced into! You can file off the machine parts, too, which is a turn off for some people.<br /> <br /> It's a big enemy that you can't defeat, like the Cthulhu Mythos, but can delay, harry and win tiny victories over which gives your players the rewards they need and keeps the horror angle intact (well, you can defeat it and one of the GMC book's hooks gives you the option, but generally it's not presented that way). It can be used to justify very, very weird goings on such as time travel, cryptids, multiple dimensions...<br /> <br /> What is the God-Machine? A toy. A framing device. A deus ex machina in every single way. And it's yours to customise (or ignore) into something you can work with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T15:29:32-08:00","id":15676,"title":"","content":"Comically enough, Deus ex Machina literally means God from the machine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T15:39:16-08:00","id":15683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/15087-sell-me-on-the-god-machine?p=15648#post15648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> A deus ex machina in every single way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware, I was punning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T11:41:53-08:00","id":16206,"title":"","content":"Hmm...with me, my appreciation of the God-Machine was such a natural thing I wouldn't know how to sell it to someone who it doesn't resonate with. Is the <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/RuleOfCool\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;Rule of Cool&quot;</a> a good enough reason? I guess for me, the God-Machine and all of the mythos surrounding it just have the right number of my favorite tropes executed in a way that just clicks with me and makes me go &quot;whoooaaaa&quot;. Maybe this is for a similar reason as Rain Neferet in that I work in IT/Business Analysis and the juxtaposition of high-concept supernatural fantasy being mixed with the terminology and concepts that I use in a system implementation with a few dashes of body horror thrown in for good measure just tickles my awesomeness bone.<br /> <br /> I do have a confession to make in that I haven't actually done a TON of roleplaying myself, so I can't say any of this from experience, but the rules and setting of GMC (and what D:tD adds to it) just have the right stuff for the stories I always wanted to run and/or be a part of. I tend to prefer mortals based games where the players have no idea what they are getting themselves into and only get to see a little of the true World of Darkness rather than being supernatural entities themselves...so the haziness in the explanation of what the GM is works just fine for me...I can kind of interpret it however I want. <br /> <br /> Like I said, it's really hard to explain why exactly I dig it so much, thus I'm not sure what exactly would change your mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1243-frothy_ham","name":"Frothy_Ham","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T11:45:29-08:00","id":16207,"title":"","content":"Similarly, as someone who has studied the theory of digital physics and finds it fascinating, the idea of a literal computer god really tickles me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T13:53:48-08:00","id":16268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frothy_Ham</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/15087-sell-me-on-the-god-machine?p=16206#post16206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Like I said, it's really hard to explain why exactly I dig it so much, thus I'm not sure what exactly would change your mind.</div> </div> </div> </div> Rule of Cool is, of course, one of the Kings of the YMMV tropes. I'm not entirely sure why I'm naturally averse to the idea of the God Machine, either. I think a lot of it is strong subconscious pushback against anything that even vaguely, conceptually associates the WoD with The Matrix, and an aversion to having a true, proximate controlling deity - even a flawed and sometimes impotent demiurge - &quot;running&quot; things (I'm also not big on grand unifying theories or &quot;the Exarchs did it&quot; either). This is probably why I like interpretations that veer more toward techno-Azathoth or reality-cancer more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T03:07:20-08:00","id":16545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>squidheadjax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/15087-sell-me-on-the-god-machine?p=16268#post16268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Rule of Cool is, of course, one of the Kings of the YMMV tropes. I'm not entirely sure why I'm naturally averse to the idea of the God Machine, either. I think a lot of it is strong subconscious pushback against anything that even vaguely, conceptually associates the WoD with The Matrix, and an aversion to having a true, proximate controlling deity - even a flawed and sometimes impotent demiurge - &quot;running&quot; things (I'm also not big on grand unifying theories or &quot;the Exarchs did it&quot; either). This is probably why I like interpretations that veer more toward techno-Azathoth or reality-cancer more.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you can argue pretty successfully that the God Machine is techno-Azathoth or reality-cancer based on the information we've been given, yeah.<br /> <br /> Anyway, based on what I've read, the God Machine is capable of making big, sweeping changes to reality, but isn't able to do fine detail without tools, much like a human can't pick up one bacterium without tools either. So that's why it has an angel nudge something to reactivate a piece of disused infrastructure rather than risk breaking the planet in half by, say, manipulating the gravitational constant of the universe in our solar system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}